  "question": {
    "text": "Given,&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo> <mo>+</mo> <mn>3</mn> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo> <mo>→</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>NH</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo> <mtext>;</mtext></mrow></math><br />\r<math> <msub> <mo>Δ</mo> <mtext>r</mtext> </msub> <msup> <mtext>H</mtext> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mn>9</mn> <mn>2</mn> <mo>·</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">kJ</mi> <mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace> <msup> <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mol</mi> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </math><br />\r<br />\rWhat is the magnitude of standard enthalpy of formation of NH<sub>3</sub> gas?"
